---
import Layout from "../../../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="FAQs – CENIT e.V."
  canonical="https://cenit-ev.de/en/faqs/"
  bodyClass="page-faqs"
>
<!-- =========================
     FAQS – INTRO / HERO IMAGE (internal)
========================= -->
<section class="cenit-section page-faqs-hero">
  <div class="cenit-container">
    <div class="cenit-heroimg reveal" style="--reveal-delay:0ms">
      <img
        src="/assets/img/hero-taenzerin.jpg"
        alt="Abstract black and white dance photography"
        loading="eager">
      <div class="cenit-heroimg-overlay">
        <h1 class="cenit-heroimg-title reveal" style="--reveal-delay:140ms">
          
          <span data-lang="en">Frequently Asked Questions</span>
        </h1>
        <p class="cenit-lead reveal" style="--reveal-delay:220ms; text-align:left; margin:0;">
          
          <span data-lang="en">
            Here we answer key questions about CENIT, our work, and our non-profit mission.
            Clear, transparent, and without unnecessary jargon.
          </span>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

   <!-- ROW 1 -->
<div class="cenit-faq-row reveal" style="--reveal-delay:80ms">
  <!-- 1 (light) -->
  <div class="cenit-faq-card is-light">
    <h3 class="cenit-faq-q">
      
      <span data-lang="en">How is CENIT different from existing networks?</span>
    </h3>
    <p class="cenit-text">
      
      <span data-lang="en">
        CENIT is not merely a networking format. We are a non-profit support association with a clear mandate:
        strengthening prevention in dance as an effective, evidence-based part of dance practice.
      </span>
    </p>
    <ul class="cenit-faq-list">
      <li>
        
        <span data-lang="en">We bring scientific evidence into dialogue with payers and institutions.</span>
      </li>
      <li>
        
        <span data-lang="en">We are not interest-driven; we are public-benefit oriented.</span>
      </li>
      <li>
        
        <span data-lang="en">We focus on sustainable structures—not short-term initiatives.</span>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </div>
  <!-- 2 (dark) -->
  <div class="cenit-faq-card is-dark">
    <h3 class="cenit-faq-q">
      
      <span data-lang="en">What makes CENIT special?</span>
    </h3>
    <p class="cenit-text">
      
      <span data-lang="en">
        CENIT connects people and organizations dedicated to dance-medicine prevention. We support ideas—from workshops
        and scientific studies to network-building.
      </span>
    </p>
    <p class="cenit-text" style="margin-top:10px;">
      
      <span data-lang="en">We support partners who …</span>
    </p>
    <ul class="cenit-faq-list">
      <li>
        
        <span data-lang="en">translate scientific insights,</span>
      </li>
      <li>
        
        <span data-lang="en">embed prevention in training and practice,</span>
      </li>
      <li>
        
        <span data-lang="en">enable dance-medicine research,</span>
      </li>
      <li>
        
        <span data-lang="en">make healthy dancing accessible across age groups.</span>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</div>
<!-- ROW 2 -->
<div class="cenit-faq-row reveal" style="--reveal-delay:140ms">
  <!-- 3 (dark) -->
  <div class="cenit-faq-card is-dark">
    <h3 class="cenit-faq-q">
      
      <span data-lang="en">Why do we focus on prevention in dance?</span>
    </h3>
    <p class="cenit-text">
      
      <span data-lang="en">
        Dancers belong to professional and activity groups with a high risk of injury and overload.
        We aim to help prevent these burdens before they occur.
      </span>
    </p>
    <ul class="cenit-faq-list">
      <li>
        
        <span data-lang="en">Prevention reduces injury risks and overload,</span>
      </li>
      <li>
        
        <span data-lang="en">it supports longer active careers,</span>
      </li>
      <li>
        
        <span data-lang="en">it reduces healthcare costs,</span>
      </li>
      <li>
        
        <span data-lang="en">it is more sustainable than treatment alone.</span>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </div>
  <!-- 4 (light) -->
  <div class="cenit-faq-card is-light">
    <h3 class="cenit-faq-q">
      
      <span data-lang="en">How does CENIT sustain its work?</span>
    </h3>
    <p class="cenit-text">
      
      <span data-lang="en">
        Our work is funded through membership fees, donations, and project-based support.
        All funds go directly into our core work:
      </span>
    </p>
    <ul class="cenit-faq-list">
      <li>
        
        <span data-lang="en">education and knowledge transfer,</span>
      </li>
      <li>
        
        <span data-lang="en">building collaborations,</span>
      </li>
      <li>
        
        <span data-lang="en">enabling research – for example, by making the right funding programs visible.</span>
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p class="cenit-text" style="margin-top:10px;">
      
      <span data-lang="en">We act independently and without any sovereign authority.</span>
    </p>
  </div>
</div>
<!-- ROW 3 -->
<div class="cenit-faq-row reveal" style="--reveal-delay:200ms">
  <!-- 5 (light) -->
  <div class="cenit-faq-card is-light">
    <h3 class="cenit-faq-q">
      
      <span data-lang="en">How can I become part of this movement?</span>
    </h3>
    <p class="cenit-text">
      
      <span data-lang="en">There are several ways to actively support CENIT:</span>
    </p>
    <ul class="cenit-faq-list">
      <li>
        
        <span data-lang="en">Membership (individual or institution),</span>
      </li>
      <li>
        
        <span data-lang="en">Project support or donations,</span>
      </li>
      <li>
        
        <span data-lang="en">Initiating collaborations (e.g., research projects or prevention programs).</span>
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p class="cenit-text" style="margin-top:10px;">
      
      <span data-lang="en">
        Every form of support strengthens prevention across the dance field—from early childhood to older adulthood.
      </span>
    </p>
  </div>
  <!-- 6 (dark) -->
  <div class="cenit-faq-card is-dark">
    <h3 class="cenit-faq-q">
      
      <span data-lang="en">How does CENIT put science into motion?</span>
    </h3>
    <p class="cenit-text">
      
      <span data-lang="en">
        We work to make scientific insights visible, accessible, and usable.
      </span>
    </p>
    <ul class="cenit-faq-list">
      <li>
        
        <span data-lang="en">Supporting and initiating studies on prevention in dance,</span>
      </li>
      <li>
        
        <span data-lang="en">Collaborating with universities, clinics, and research groups,</span>
      </li>
      <li>
        
        <span data-lang="en">Translating and sharing scientific insights,</span>
      </li>
      <li>
        
        <span data-lang="en">Publishing work that demonstrates the benefits of preventive measures.</span>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</div>
<!-- ROW 4 (wide) -->
<div class="cenit-faq-row cenit-faq-row--wide reveal" style="--reveal-delay:80ms">
  <div class="cenit-faq-card is-light">
    <h3 class="cenit-faq-q">
      
      <span data-lang="en">What CENIT does not do</span>
    </h3>
    <p class="cenit-text">
      
      <span data-lang="en">
        To avoid misunderstandings and protect our non-profit status, it’s important to clarify what we do not do:
      </span>
    </p>
    <ul class="cenit-faq-list">
      <li>
        
        <span data-lang="en">We do not represent a professional group.</span>
      </li>
      <li>
        
        <span data-lang="en">We do not engage in professional politics.</span>
      </li>
      <li>
        
        <span data-lang="en">We do not advise individual professional dancers as a trade association would.</span>
      </li>
      <li>
        
        <span data-lang="en">We do not set mandatory quality standards and we are not a certification body.</span>
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p class="cenit-text" style="margin-top:10px;">
      
      <span data-lang="en">Our mandate is to promote prevention in dance for the benefit of the public.</span>
    </p>
  </div>
</div>
      <!-- FINAL split card -->
      <div class="cenit-card cenit-faq-final reveal" style="--reveal-delay:80ms">
        <div class="cenit-faq-final-media">
          <img src="/assets/img/FotoKontakt.jpg" alt="Dance spotlight" loading="lazy">
        </div>
        <div class="cenit-faq-final-content">
          <h3 class="cenit-faq-final-title">
            
            <span data-lang="en">Do you have more questions?</span>
          </h3>
          <p class="cenit-text">
            
            <span data-lang="en">
              Don’t hesitate to reach out. We look forward to connecting and are happy to answer any questions about CENIT and our mission.
            </span>
          </p>
          <div class="cenit-faq-final-actions">
            <a href="/en/satzung#leitbild" class="cenit-btn cenit-btn--light">
              
              <span data-lang="en">Our full mission statement</span>
            </a>
            <a href="/en/#kontakt" class="cenit-btn cenit-btn--light">
              
              <span data-lang="en">Get in touch</span>
            </a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

</Layout>

<style>
  /* Fix: in der breiten Reihe ("Was CENIT nicht macht") zentriert eine
     max-width/margin:auto-Regel aus main.css die <p>-Texte, während die
     <ul> davon unberührt bleibt – dadurch wirken Ein-/Ausleitung eingerückt. */
  .cenit-faq-row--wide .cenit-faq-card .cenit-text {
    max-width: none;
    margin-left: 0;
    margin-right: 0;
  }
</style>
